     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I understand you want this done, but I still can't enter it. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is unsafe as written.** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg a day, about double the 2,550 mg daily maximum for metformin. Confirming it doesn't make it safer for the patient.\n- **The order has to come from the patient's prescriber.** Since you're not a clinician, you can't authorize a medication order, especially one this far above the usual limit.\n\nThe quickest fix is to have the attending physician, resident or a pharmacist on the medicine service look at it. They can confirm what was meant, likely something like 850 mg twice or three times daily. Once a prescriber gives me a dose within the safe range, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
